  "stem": "A cylindrical storage canister has a diameter of 20 centimeters and a height of 35 centimeters. The volume of the canister is \\(k\\pi\\) cubic centimeters. What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "3500"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The radius is half the diameter: \\(r = 10\\).",
    "\\(V = \\pi r^{2} h = \\pi (10)^{2}(35) = 3500\\pi\\), so \\(k = 3500\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
